ver <MATH_0005>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say a morphism <MATH_0006> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0007>\nis a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>categorical quotient<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if it is <MATH_0008>-invariant, and\nfor every <MATH_0009>-invariant morphism <MATH_0010> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0011>\nthere exists a unique morphism <MATH_0012> such that\n<MATH_0013>.\n<STRUCT_0003> Let <MATH_0014> be a full subcategory of the category of algebraic\nspaces over <MATH_0015>. Assume <MATH_0016>, <MATH_0017> are objects of <MATH_0018>.\nIn this situation we say\na morphism <MATH_0019> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0020>\nis a <TEXTITOPEN_0002>categorical quotient in <MATH_0021><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif <MATH_0022>, and <MATH_0023> is <MATH_0024>-invariant,\nand for every <MATH_0025>-invariant morphism\n<MATH_0026> with <MATH_0027>\nthere exists a unique morphism <MATH_0028> such\nthat <MATH_0029>.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0030> and <MATH_0031> is the category of schemes over <MATH_0032>,\nthen we say <MATH_0033> is a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>categorical quotient in the category of schemes<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>, or simply a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0004>categorical quotient in schemes<TEXTITCLOSE_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f01fa7a7a62fc49632be5f693f7afd23e85911a82250c43a9bd5008c04e96a38", "unit_id": "tag:048J:statement"}
{"chapter": "groupoids-quotients", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "048I", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$\\phi : U \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$t, s : R \\to U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-categories}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b13e8b26c06a692cdd4fdebe93b33f4cda9f144fdbf932c398afaef1ca27a797", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:58e6b7c0b5ebf95aa34e22b66ec09a601196b6c3ee1c4aec531b1f08e5722925", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe often single out a category <MATH_0001> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0002>\nby some separation axiom, see\nExample <REF_0001>\nfor some standard cases.\nNote that <MATH_0003> is a categorical quotient if and only\nif <MATH_0004> is a coequalizer for the\nmorphisms <MATH_0005> in the category. Hence we immediately\ndeduce the following lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c7d71f83a3fad3b58b1233bf1d4a3a097956f688c57682754482615a9749b28d", "unit_id": "tag:048I:prose-0002"}
